<title>CANADA: UGG calls meeting on rights plan.</title>
<headline>UGG calls meeting on rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain handler United Grain Growers Ltd said it called a special meeting of shareholders for Thursday, June 26 in Winnipeg after a request by New York-based investment firm Oppenheimer &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Oppenheimer, which owns about 5.5 percent of UGG's common shares, wants the meeting to submit its shareholder rights plan to shareholders for approval, consider whether to allow UGG's board from implementing a similar plan without approval, and consider amending a special act of parliament under which UGG is incorporated to limit the number of shares issued to the level of April 9, 1997.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
